            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:label>W_G2D</rdfs:label>
        <skos:definition>W_G2D is the second state-variable of the Generic 2-Dimensional Oscillator model, that can be associated with accommodation and refractoriness and considered to represent potassium activation, sodium inactivation, or both (FitzHugh, 1961).

W_G2D is a more slower changing variable than V_G2D (the parameter introducing this time-scale separation is tau_G2D ≥ 1).</skos:definition>
        <category>State-Variable</category>
        <category>StateVariable</category>
        <identifier>000917</identifier>
        <references>FitzHugh, R. *Impulses and physiological states in theoretical models of nerve membrane*, Biophysical Journal 1: 445, 1961.</references>
        <stateVariableRange>-6.0, 6.0</stateVariableRange>
        <symbol>W</symbol>
    </owl:Class>
    


