                <owl:hasValue rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/tvbo/Breaksetal_2003_b"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:label>delta_V_LB</rdfs:label>
        <skos:altLabel>d_V_LB</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:definition>Variance of excitatory threshold. Defines the steepness of sigmoid $Q_V$.</skos:definition>
        <category>Parameter</category>
        <defaultValue>0.65</defaultValue>
        <defaultValue rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">0.65</defaultValue>
        <dynamicsExploration>Breakspear et al. 2003b:

Dynamics exploration of local uncoupled columns (C_LB = 0) and coupled columns (C_LB &gt; 0) using delta_V_LB as control parameter.

For local uncoupled columns (C_LB = 0):

Fixed point attractors for delta_V_LB &lt; 0.55
Limit cycle attractors for 0.55 &lt; delta_V_LB &lt; 0.59
Chaotic attractors for delta_V_LB &gt; 0.59</dynamicsExploration>
        <identifier>001096</identifier>
        <identifier>001106</identifier>
        <range>lo=0.49, hi=0.7, step=0.01</range>
        <shortName>Exc. mean threshold variance</shortName>
        <symbol>\delta_{V}</symbol>
        <symbol>delta_V</symbol>
        <tvbSourceVariable>d_V</tvbSourceVariable>
    </owl:Class>
    


