                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/tvbo/x2dot_E5D"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:label>g_E5D</rdfs:label>
        <skos:definition>g_E5D is a low-pass filtered excitatory coupling function from sub-population (x1_E5D, y1_E5D) to (x2_E5D, y2_E5D) in Epileptor5D (Jirsa et al.,2014).

This coupling function has been introduced in the uncoupled model (i.e., zero coupling between the two sub-populations) in order to generate spike-and-wave events and interictal spikes.</skos:definition>
        <category>State Variable</category>
        <category>StateVariable</category>
        <identifier>001156</identifier>
