        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:label>lamda_RWW_EI</rdfs:label>
        <skos:definition>Inhibitory global coupling scaling</skos:definition>
        <skos:definition>The parameter lambda_RWW_EI indicates whether long-range feedforward inhibition (FFI) is considered (lamba = 1) or not (lambda = 0) (Deco et al., 2014).

Note:
- In the case of FFI, the proportion of excitatory–inhibitory long-range connections and excitatory–excitatory long-range connections is the same.</skos:definition>
        <category>Parameter</category>
        <defaultValue>0.0</defaultValue>
        <defaultValue rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</defaultValue>
        <identifier>001209</identifier>
        <range>lo=0.0, hi=1.0, step=0.01</range>
        <references>(Deco et al., 2014) Deco G, Ponce-Alvarez A, Hagmann P, Romani GL, Mantini D, Corbetta M. How local excitation–inhibition ratio impacts the whole-brain dynamics. J Neurosci, 2014 34(23): 7886-7898.</references>
        <symbol>\lambda</symbol>
        <synonym>lambda</synonym>
        <synonym>lamda</synonym>
    </owl:Class>
    


