        <rdfs:label>sigma_y0_3_JR</rdfs:label>
        <skos:definition>Sigmoid function that transforms the average membrane potential of the PCs populations (y0) into an average firing rate to the inhibitory interneurons IINs.</skos:definition>
        <category>Derived Variable</category>
        <category>Function</category>
        <equation>sigm_y0_3 = \dfrac{2*\nu_{max}}{1 + \exp(r * {v_{0} - (a_{3} * J * y_{0})})}</equation>
        <functionType>Sigmoid function</functionType>
        <identifier>001388</identifier>
        <references>(Jansen et al., 1993) Jansen BH, Zouridakis G, and Brandt M. A neurophysiologically-based mathematical model of flash visual evoked potentials. Biol. Cybern. 68, 275:283, 1993.

(Jansen &amp; Rit, 1995) Jansen BH and Rit VG. Electroencephalogram and visual evoked potential generation in a mathematical model of coupled cortical columns. Biol. Cybern. 73, 357:366, 1995.</references>
        <shortName>Potential-to-rate operator</shortName>
        <symbol>S[\alpha_{3}y_{0}]</symbol>
