                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/tvbo/zdot_E2D"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:label>z_E2D</rdfs:label>
        <skos:definition>Slow permittivity state-variable of the Epileptor2D (Proix et al.,2014).

The state-variable z_E2D is responsible for leading the autonomous switch between the interictal (between seizures) and ictal (during seizures) states on a slow time scale.

Note: This switch is accompanied by a direct current (DC) shift which has been recorded in vitro and in vivo.</skos:definition>
        <category>State Variable</category>
        <category>StateVariable</category>
        <identifier>001598</identifier>
        <references>(Proix et al., 2014) Proix, T.; Bartolomei, F; Chauvel, P; Bernard, C; Jirsa, V.K. Permittivity coupling across brain regions determines seizure recruitment in partial epilepsy. J Neurosci 2014, 34:15009-21.</references>
        <stateVariableRange>2.0, 5.0</stateVariableRange>
        <symbol>z</symbol>
    </owl:Class>
    


